    <briefdescription>
<para>FIFO container safe for concurrent producers and consumers. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Every operation takes a single mutex, so the queue can be shared between threads without external synchronisation. <ref refid="classThreadSafeQueue_1af63a11e90a58a5988cfe41a5d6aea73d" kindref="member">pop()</ref> and <ref refid="classThreadSafeQueue_1a33be668a849175ebee2439b3a3facaf2" kindref="member">front()</ref> return std::nullopt immediately when empty: there is no condition variable, so callers never wait for an element to arrive. <ref refid="classThreadSafeQueue_1a33be668a849175ebee2439b3a3facaf2" kindref="member">front()</ref> returns a copy rather than a reference, keeping the result valid after the lock is released. <parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Element type; must be copyable (front) and movable (pop, rvalue push). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="note"><para><ref refid="classThreadSafeQueue_1a58b5532baa6110071f697ad1f9bfbf58" kindref="member">empty()</ref> and <ref refid="classThreadSafeQueue_1ab255a078bfa2253878a2e17fd5a7a21c" kindref="member">size()</ref> report a snapshot; another thread can modify the queue as soon as the call returns. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
